-- title:
--   Unramified base change: e=1 and f∣[L:K]
-- statement:
--   Let $K$, $L$, $K'$, $M$ be number fields equipped with algebra structures $K\to L$, $K\to K'$, $K\to M$, $L\to M$, $K'\to M$ making $K\subseteq L\subseteq M$ and $K\subseteq K'\subseteq M$ towers, and assume $L/K$ is Galois. Suppose $\operatorname{finrank}_{K'}M=\operatorname{finrank}_K L$, and that every $x\in M$ lies in the $K'$-subalgebra generated by the image of $L$ in $M$ (so $M$ is the compositum of $K'$ and $L$, linearly disjoint over $K$, i.e. $M/K'$ is the base change of $L/K$). Let $v$ be a height-one prime of the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_K$, and assume that for every height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$ whose contraction to $\mathcal{O}_K$ is $v$ one has $\operatorname{ramificationIdx}'(v,w)=1$, i.e. $v$ is unramified in $L$. Let $\mathfrak v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{K'}$ contracting to $v$, and $\mathfrak w$ a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_M$ contracting to $\mathfrak v$. Then the ramification index of $\mathfrak w$ over $\mathfrak v$ equals $1$, and the inertia degree (residue degree) of $\mathfrak w$ over $\mathfrak v$ divides $\operatorname{finrank}_K L=[L:K]$.
--
--   This is the standard statement that unramifiedness is preserved under base change of a Galois extension along a linearly disjoint extension, together with the bound $f\mid[L:K]$ coming from $efg=[M:K']$ for the Galois extension $M/K'$; for $[L:K]$ prime it says that the completed extension $M_{\mathfrak w}/K'_{\mathfrak v}$ is either trivial or the unramified extension of degree $[L:K]$. It feeds the local computations of norms in unramified extensions used in the base-change arguments, being cited by [`IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.exists_units_prod_tensor_map_iterate_eq_tmul_one_of_finrank_dvd_valuation_norm`](thm.html#IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.exists_units_prod_tensor_map_iterate_eq_tmul_one_of_finrank_dvd_valuation_norm) and [`IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.exists_valued_eq_exp_inertiaDeg_mul_of_valued_norm_eq_of_baseChange`](thm.html#IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.exists_valued_eq_exp_inertiaDeg_mul_of_valued_norm_eq_of_baseChange).
